{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: BR-9, deployed room migration lists pinned. Head ef59a35d7ba1c22dc9fb60c9bc580d232df472e0, tree b0bf49b3395025915d3d953276ac14bae99691fd, branch request/br9-migration-prefixes-20261026: three commits on Main 9daa037e, three paths, all three named by the artifacts. Review request 471e8fc5, checker promise 049059fb, request eca4329c (builder promise 0ba038af).\n\nRead order: the primary note at the head in full; request eca4329c and finding L5-04; the test diff; the four room configuration files at Main; then the evidence.\n\nAcceptance (\"A config test fails on any change to a deployed room file's migrations list except an appended step\"): met. packages/cli/test/demo-config.test.ts pins the migration lists of apps/room/wrangler.jsonc, wrangler.grow.jsonc, wrangler.lending.jsonc and wrangler.demo.jsonc as prefixes and compares each with isDeepStrictEqual, so a removed, rewritten, inserted or reordered step fails and an appended step passes. I parsed the four files at the current Main d36773b3 with the test's own comment stripping: each list equals its pinned prefix exactly, tag by tag and class by class. Those four are the only deployed room files with migrations; the only other file with a migrations list, apps/room/lanes/wrangler.test.jsonc, is a test configuration.\n\nBase. The head sits on 9daa037e, not on Main d36773b3. Main has since gained R7 (6852f78d) and its note follow-up (d36773b3). None of those commits touches the test file or the four room configuration files (the only configuration change, the R2 binding in lanes/wrangler.test.jsonc, is outside this test's scope), and git merge-tree merges the head onto d36773b3 with no conflict. Because the test reads the configuration files at run time and they are byte-identical on both bases, the gate on the old base is valid for the composed result; no combined-head gate is claimed or owed.\n\nHead and gate. The head differs from the gated checkpoint f4735c54 (tree 849083ea) only in the note and manifest, so the documents-only rule applies. Gate V1 failed before any test (pretest refused a symlinked node_modules root) and stays recorded as failed; the repair moved the same private dependency copy to a real node_modules path, with no source change and no install. Gate V2 passed every step.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The pins are hard-coded copies of the deployed history, not derived from the current files, which is what makes a rewrite detectable. Each Worker keeps its own tag scheme. Replacing the old flattened class-set assertion for demo is correct: the new prefix check is strictly stronger and still covers the same four classes.\n\nSecurity: no change to runtime, configuration, secrets or deployment. The test guards against a migration rewrite that would break or reset Durable Object storage on deploy, which is the operational risk L5-04 names.\n\nSimplification: good. One helper, one data table and one test case, with no new parser or runner. The note's open limit is right: the test checks source files only, not the provider's deployed migration history.\n\nEvidence, verified by me:\n- Manifest digest 25a44b31… matches the request. All 68 files match their size and SHA-256 digest; nothing in /Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-10-26-br9-migration-prefixes-delivery is writable (0 of 75 entries); all 67 SHA256SUMS lines pass.\n- gate-v2/result.json records head f4735c54, tree 849083ea, main before 9daa037e and exit 0. gate.log shows changed files 0, install skipped against the lockfile, every step at exit 0, notes 0 warnings, Node 56 and Counting 55 passed, plain 2,817 passed and 1 skipped, native 771 passed and 2 skipped.\n- The control output ends with AssertionError \"wrangler.jsonc: expected false to be true\" and DISTINGUISHES, so the new assertion detects a rewritten tag that the old class-set check would have missed. I read the records; I did not rerun the control.\n- I ran the whole owning file at the head in the builder's worktree: 2 passed, and the worktree stayed clean.\n- The note is 8,245 bytes. Commit subjects are 52 to 55 characters, and git diff --check is clean.\n\nNote for the planner: when a reviewed deployment appends a migration step, the same head should append it to the pinned table, as the note says.\n\nVerdict: approved at exact head ef59a35d / tree b0bf49b3. The builder lands. No deployment.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2280e436d5057d69a199f57129b34ded50f9fcba","binding":"assigned","head":"ef59a35d7ba1c22dc9fb60c9bc580d232df472e0","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:049059fb076e58963b5dfeb62548e66cd0df6beb\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0ba038af99bea47894bfb4375d529b86ae436e81\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:049059fb076e58963b5dfeb62548e66cd0df6beb","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}